# Commercial S3.1 allowlist hash query diagnosis

Date: 2026-08-29

A read-only SSH revalidation correctly confirmed the allowlist metadata,
inactive/dead service state, zero restart count, zero main PID and valid
recovery checksums. The two displayed SHA-256 fields were empty because the
local command over-escaped the remote awk field expression. No file, service,
repository, database or evidence was changed. The hash-only query is repeated
with fixed-width extraction and no secret or private Telegram identifier
output.
